  "title": "text2pcap: Use -F flag for tests",
  "description": "Use the -F file type flag to have the text2pcap tests produce the\nsame file type as the input flag, which is a little superior when\nthe input flag is a nanosecond pcap.\n\nNote that commit 5076aee04431c123b81d0a9e3d69571a4572999a means that\ncapinfos -M provides a machine-readable filetype that's easier to put\nback into text2pcap.",
